# Baseline allow-list for scripts/forbid_page_title_token_fork.sh Rule A.
#
# Every *Title-suffixed static TextStyle token on VelvetText that legitimately
# exists for something OTHER than a bottom-nav tab-root page title (card
# titles, calendar nav titles, passport section titles, ...). One name per
# line; `#` starts a reason comment. `pageTitle` itself is the canonical
# token and is always implicitly allowed — do not list it here.
#
# A NEW name appearing on this list is a signal to double-check: is this
# really a distinct concern, or is it the same "per-screen one-off" shape
# that caused the original divergence (masterBookingsTitle, now deleted)? If
# it is genuinely a page title, point it at VelvetText.pageTitle instead of
# adding a new token here.

cardTitle          # per-card heading inside a list item, not a screen title
monthNavTitle      # calendar month-nav header, not a screen title
dayHeaderTitle     # day-group header inside a booking list, not a screen title
homePassportPreviewTitle  # Beauty Passport home-card preview heading
passportSectionTitle      # Beauty Passport section heading
passportFooterTitle       # Beauty Passport footer heading
